# Example requests for the Ticket Analysis API (VS Code REST Client extension: click "Send Request").
# Start the API first: python -m api --local   (or --auth api_key for the key examples, or docker compose up)
# Made-up text only. @apiKey is used only when the API runs with AUTH_MODE=api_key.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@apiKey = paste-the-API_KEYS-value-from-.env

### Liveness and readiness (no auth)
GET {{base}}/health

###
GET {{base}}/ready

### Detect: subject and zendeskOrgId (integer)
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-Request-Id: example-detect-1

{
  "text": "The REPORTS instance on FAKESQL01 is slow since this morning. FAKESQL02\\FINANCE is fine.",
  "subject": "Slow reports",
  "zendeskOrgId": 999001,
  "ticketId": "12345"
}

### Detect: text only, no subject and no client (no client's known names apply)
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "Please check FAKESQL01 and FAKESQL01\\REPORTS today."
}

### Detect: zendeskOrgId as a string
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "Server=FAKESQL03,1433;Database=FAKE_DB is refusing connections.",
  "zendeskOrgId": "999001"
}

### Classify: the access request email (rule:access_request)
POST {{base}}/v1/classify
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "Hi Fortified Data Support,\r\n\r\nCould you please help me get READ access for the schema below, Server=FAKESQL01, Database=FAKE_DB, for the execution user CORP\\svc-fake-batch. Please approve.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJane Doe\r\nData Engineer | Fake Co",
  "subject": "READ access request"
}

### Classify: without a subject
POST {{base}}/v1/classify
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "Disk space is low on the data drive of FAKESQL01, the volume is nearly full."
}

### Analyze: a collector alert (alert-name table, alert intent rule)
POST {{base}}/v1/analyze
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "text": "AlertId 123456\nAlert FD - SQL Agent Job Failure\nClient Name Fake Co\nServer FAKESQL01\nPlatform Microsoft SQL Server\nInstance Job: Nightly Load, Category: Data\nMessage Error: The job failed.\nSeverity Warning\nLevel Failure\nPreviousLevel OK\nOpen Date 07/21/2026 17:00:00 UTC\n",
  "subject": "Fake Co - Alert #42 - FD - SQL Agent Job Failure",
  "zendeskOrgId": 999001
}

### Catalog: every key and value the responses can contain
GET {{base}}/v1/catalog
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Auth failure: a wrong key (401 when the API runs with --auth api_key)
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: fake-wrong-key-0000000000

{
  "text": "FAKESQL01 is down."
}

### Validation failure: no text (422)
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "subject": "No text"
}

### Oversized body (413): the REST Client cannot generate 1 MB, so use docs/api-examples.ps1 for this case.
# A body that is not JSON gives 415:
POST {{base}}/v1/detect
Content-Type: text/plain
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

FAKESQL01 is down.
